## 2. Why `2x2` `Grid4` Generation + `V0_OrthoIsoGate` Solves Both Hard-Surface & Organic Isolation

Examining validated [`neighbor_crown_grid4_V5.png`](/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-meshes/Projects/14_ArmGuard_13-November-2026/components/Arm_Flare/isolation/I_009_14-November-2026-0238/neighbor_crown_grid4_V5.png) and [`neighbor_forearm_grid4_V5.png`](/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-meshes/Projects/14_ArmGuard_13-November-2026/components/Arm_Flare/isolation/I_009_14-November-2026-0238/neighbor_forearm_grid4_V5.png) confirms why generating a single `2x2` sheet (`TL=Front, TR=Back, BL=Left, BR=Top`, extensible to `3x2` with `Bottom`) performs dramatically better:
- Shared canvas latent attention enforces identical clay tone, directional softness, and approximate scale in one shot.
- Adding a **coarse 3D Depth + Edge Proxy `grid4` plate** as Reference #1 (`PromptGridV6_ProxyGuided.md`) eliminates the final failure mode (oblique camera hallucination on `left`/`top`), because Control/reference conditioning fixes the camera angle mathematically instead of relying on French prose (`"ce n'est PAS la vue de face"`).

Even before changing the generator model, adding a pure-CV **`V0_OrthoIsoGate`** check (<100 ms per kit inside `GeminiBridge.py` `/save` and `OnePictureIsolate.py`) catches bad lots deterministically:

| Gate Metric (`V0_OrthoIsoGate`) | Threshold | What It Catches Immediately |
|---|---|---|
| **G0.1 Square Aspect** | `abs(W/H - 1.0) <= 0.02` | Rejects `0.750` portrait (`I_008/left`) and `2.000` landscape (`I_008/top`) |
| **G0.2 Background Uniformity** | `std(bg_border) <= 4.0` & `1` main island | Rejects textured floors, shadows, and multiple stray neighbor shards |
| **G0.3 Mirror Silhouette IoU (`Front` vs `flip_x(Back)`)** | Normalized BBox IoU `>= 0.78` | Catches mismatched outer notches, tilted poses, or hallucinated horns |
| **G0.4 Epipolar Height Span (`Front` vs `Back`, `Front` vs `Left`)** | Relative height ratio in `[0.88, 1.14]` | Rejects oblique tilted side/front mismatches before contour tracing |
| **G0.5 Epipolar Width Span (`Front` vs `Top`)** | Relative width ratio in `[0.88, 1.14]` | Rejects unaligned `top` arches that widen or narrow vs `front` |
| **G0.6 Light Direction Flatness (`CheckAiHeight`)** | Interior directional coherence `<= 0.25` | Flags dramatic spotlight shading that biases CMY Yellow extraction |

